#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:220
msgid "The Export Engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:222
msgid ""
"The crown jewel of `llvm-export` is its export module (`crates/llvm-export/"
"src/export/`) -- the code that converts a pliron IR module into valid "
"textual LLVM IR. This is the part cuda-oxide keeps local: pliron-llvm only "
"emits real `.ll` via an `llvm-sys` bridge, which cuda-oxide avoids. This is "
"not just \"print each operation\"; several non-trivial transformations "
"happen during export:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:229
msgid ""
"**Block arguments become PHI nodes.** Pliron IR (MLIR-like) models merge "
"points as block arguments -- a function-style calling convention between "
"basic blocks. LLVM IR uses PHI nodes instead. The exporter builds a "
"predecessor map from branch operands and emits `phi` instructions at the top "
"of each non-entry block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:235
msgid ""
"**Value naming.** A pre-pass assigns sequential SSA names (`%v0`, "
"`%v1`, ...) to every value. Constants are special-cased: `llvm.constant` "
"results are mapped to their literal value (not a `%vN` name), so PHIs can "
"reference constants from blocks that appear later in the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:240
msgid ""
"**NVVM intrinsic name conversion.** Pliron identifiers use underscores; LLVM "
"intrinsics use dots. The exporter converts all names starting with `llvm_` "
"by replacing underscores with dots: `llvm_nvvm_read_ptx_sreg_tid_x` becomes "
"`llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x`. This is a mechanical transformation, not a "
"lookup table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:246
msgid ""
"**Convergent attribute marking.** Barrier, shuffle, and vote intrinsics must "
"be marked `convergent` to prevent LLVM from hoisting them out of control "
"flow. The exporter recognizes these by prefix pattern matching on the (dot-"
"form) name and appends `#0` to their call sites, emitting `attributes #0 = "
"{ convergent }` at module level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:252
msgid ""
"**Kernel metadata.** Functions marked as kernels get `ptx_kernel` calling "
"convention and an `!nvvm.annotations` metadata entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:255
msgid ""
"Here is what the exported LLVM IR looks like for a simple vector-add kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:257
msgid ""
"target datalayout = \"e-i64:64-i128:128-v16:16-v32:32-n16:32:64\"\n"
"target triple = \"nvptx64-nvidia-cuda\"\n"
"\n"
"declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n"
"declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()\n"
"declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()\n"
"\n"
"define ptx_kernel void @vecadd(ptr addrspace(1) %v0, i64 %v1,\n"
"                                ptr addrspace(1) %v2, i64 %v3,\n"
"                                ptr addrspace(1) %v4, i64 %v5) {\n"
"entry:\n"
"    %v6 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x() #0\n"
"    %v7 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x() #0\n"
"    %v8 = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x() #0\n"
"    %v9 = mul i32 %v8, %v7\n"
"    %v10 = add i32 %v9, %v6\n"
"    ; ... bounds check, load, add, store ...\n"
"    ret void\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"!nvvm.annotations = !{!0}\n"
"!0 = !{ptr @vecadd, !\"kernel\", i32 1}\n"
"attributes #0 = { convergent }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:283
msgid ""
"Notice the slices have been scalarized: each Rust `&[f32]` becomes a `ptr "
"addrspace(1)` and an `i64` length. That happened in the lowering pass; by "
"the time the LLVM dialect sees them, they are flat arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:289
msgid "dialect-nvvm -- The GPU Layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:291
msgid ""
"`dialect-nvvm` wraps NVIDIA's GPU intrinsics as typed pliron operations. "
"These operations do not form a \"level\" in the lowering chain -- they are "
"inserted during the `dialect-mir` → LLVM dialect lowering pass and coexist "
"with LLVM dialect operations in the same function body. At export time, they "
"become `call` instructions to `@llvm.nvvm.*` intrinsics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../compiler/mlir-dialects.md:297
